{
  "manufacturer": "Price Industries",
  "manufacturer_slug": "price-industries",
  "model": "PRTU Price Rooftop Unit Controller",
  "model_slug": "prtu",
  "aliases": [
    "PRTU",
    "Price Rooftop Unit Controller",
    "PRTU-STAT"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Rooftop unit controller (zoning / voting)",
  "applies_to": "Packaged single- and multi-stage rooftop units (about 2-30 tons) run by a Price PRTU, alone or polling Price zone controllers.",
  "summary": "The PRTU is a Price controller that stages a packaged rooftop unit (up to 4 cooling and 4 heating stages plus fan) from its own thermostat or from zone demand. In networked mode it polls up to 30 Price PIC controllers or Prodigy diffusers over BACnet MS/TP every 3 minutes and picks the rooftop mode by voting; if polling fails it drops to standalone. A BMS reaches it on the same BACnet MS/TP trunk as the zone controllers.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "v1.8.0",
  "default_device_instance": 100,
  "notes": [
    "AV 4 and AV 5 are both printed as \"Day Minimum Setpoint\"; by their defaults (65°F and 80°F) and ranges AV 5 is the upper limit.",
    "The source prints AI0 for the AI10 spare input and A02 for AO2; listed here as AI 10 and AO 2.",
    "MV 6 has no name in the source (N/A, states One-Four).",
    "Reset counters (AV 34-41) and zone bit-flag words (AV 42-49) are marked for internal use; convert the flags to binary to read them per zone.",
    "Polled demands (AV 10-12) are the share of zones calling for cooling, heating or deadband."
  ],
